{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-es-pro-1-7","title":"Proverbios 1:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Introducción al libro - Proverbios Lea el primer capítulo de Proverbios. Esta colección de dichos sentenciosos es la sabiduría divina aplicada a las condiciones terrenales del pueblo de Dios. Que los Proverbios fueran de Salomón (Proverbios 1:1) no implica más que que reunió en forma ordenada dichos ya corrientes entre la gente, la sabiduría del Espíritu, tal vez a lo largo de muchos siglos (Eclesiastés 12:9). Los capítulos 25-29 estaban vigentes en la época de Ezequías (Eclesiastés 25:1). Los capítulos 30 y 31 son de Agur y Lemuel. El libro consta de seis partes: A los hijos, 1-7. La alabanza de la sabiduría, 8-9. La locura del pecado, 10-19. Advertencias e instrucciones, 20-29. Las palabras de Agur, 30. Las palabras del rey Lemuel, 31. Temor también; Proverbios 1:29, (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 19:9&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-1-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-1-12","title":"Proverbios 1:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>tumba heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-1-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-1-29","title":"Proverbios 1:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>miedo También; Proverbios 1:7. (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-1-29","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-2-5","title":"Proverbios 2:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>miedo También; Proverbios 3:7, (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-2-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-2-21","title":"Proverbios 2:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>perfecto (véase Scofield &quot;1 Reyes 8:61&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-2-21","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-3-5","title":"Proverbios 3:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>confianza (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 2:12&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-3-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-3-7","title":"Proverbios 3:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>miedo También; Proverbios 2:5 (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 19:9&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-3-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-5-5","title":"Proverbios 5:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>infierno heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-5-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-7-27","title":"Proverbios 7:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>infierno heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-7-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-8-1","title":"Proverbios 8:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>infierno heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-8-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-8-13","title":"Proverbios 8:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 19:9&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-8-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-8-22","title":"Proverbios 8:22","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>El Señor me poseyó. Que la sabiduría es más que la personificación de un atributo de Dios, o de la voluntad de Dios como lo mejor para el hombre, sino que es una clara sombra de Cristo, es seguro para la mente devota. Proverbios 8:22-36; Juan 1:1-3; Colosenses 1:17 puede referirse nada menos que al Hijo Eterno de Dios.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-8-22","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-9-10","title":"Proverbios 9:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 19:9&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-9-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-9-18","title":"Proverbios 9:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>infierno heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-9-18","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-10-1","title":"Proverbios 10:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>hijo necio Un &quot;necio&quot; en la Escritura nunca es una persona mentalmente deficiente, sino alguien arrogante y autosuficiente; uno que ordena su vida como si no hubiera Dios. Véase, como ilustración, Lucas 12:16-20. El rico no era mentalmente deficiente, pero era &quot;necio&quot; porque suponía que su alma podía vivir de las cosas del granero, sin pensar en su bienestar eterno.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-10-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-10-27","title":"Proverbios 10:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmos 19:9&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-10-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-11-5","title":"Proverbios 11:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>perfecto (véase Scofield &quot;1 Reyes 8:61&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-11-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-11-25","title":"Proverbios 11:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>alma liberal Ver; 2 Corintios 9:6-10.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-11-25","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-11-28","title":"Proverbios 11:28","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>confía (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-11-28","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-14-2","title":"Proverbios 14:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>teme (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-14-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-14-26","title":"Proverbios 14:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>miedo También; Proverbios 15:16, (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-14-26","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-14-27","title":"Proverbios 14:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-14-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-15-11","title":"Proverbios 15:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>infierno heb. &quot;Seol&quot; (véase Scofield &quot;Habacuc 2:5&quot;), Job 26:6; Salmo 139:8.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-pro-15-11","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-pro-15-16","title":"P